					<![CDATA[
						 <div style="text-align: right;"></div> <p><strong>SCP-5487</strong><br /> <strong>Containment Class:</strong> Safe</p> <p><strong>Special Containment Procedures:</strong> The underground complex SCP-5487 occupies has been repurposed and designated Provisional Site-405. MTF unit Iota-27 (“Art Connoisseurs”) has been created to explore the different SCP-5487-1s generated by SCP-5487. Site-405 is to be staffed by no less than 3 security personnel, and 2 research personnel at all times.</p> <p><strong>Description:</strong> SCP-5487 is located in █████, United States. SCP-5487 resembles a Dell Dimension 4500, but it has 2 extra oddly shaped ports at the back. The first of these ports is connected by wire to a mahogany door frame, although no door is present within the frame. The second is connected to what appears to be a large scanner, about 2ft x 2ft.</p> <p>When powered on, SCP-5487 will display an interface if a monitor is connected. The interface includes variables, parameters, and measurements, as well as a button labeled as “Start” and a faded button labeled as “Stop”. When a painting is inserted into the scanner and “Start” is pressed, the doorframe will create a portal into a computer generated replica of the painting present within the scanner, hereby referred to as SCP-5487-1.</p> <p>When entered, the subject will be placed in front of the focal point of the painting, and an identical mahogany door will appear behind them. The space appears 3D, and subjects can walk into the foreground and background, as well as behind objects or off the side of what is present in the painting. There appears to be no limit to how expansive SCP-5487-1 is.</p> <p>If humans or other creatures are on the painting, they appear in SCP-5487-1 and are capable of self locomotion. Humans are capable of speaking and conscious thought. These creatures will be doing the task that they appear to be doing in the painting when the subject enters SCP-5487-1.</p> <div class="collapsible-block"> <div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Exploration&nbsp;Log&nbsp;02</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none"> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Exploration&nbsp;Log&nbsp;02</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-content"> <div class="blockquote"> <p><strong>MTF Unit:</strong> Iota-27 (“Art Connoisseurs”)<br /> <strong>MTF Squad:</strong> Delta-3<br /> <strong>SCP-5487-1:</strong> Starry Night by Van Gogh<br /> <strong>Task:</strong> Reach the edge of SCP-5487-1<br /> <strong>Foreword:</strong> Communication with individuals within SCP-5487-1 has proven impossible. The following was locally stored on the person of Lt. Johnson.</p> <p><strong>&lt;Begin Log&gt;</strong></p> <p>(Lt. Johnson, Pvt. Carter, and Pvt. Miller are audibly laughing. Sgt. Anderson is not amused.)</p> <p><strong>Sgt. Anderson:</strong> Sorry to interrupt, but something stands out about that cabin over there. It looks different than all of the other buildings we have seen before.</p> <p>(While being colored like the others, the indicated structure seems to be built with actual geometry.)</p> <p><strong>Lt. Johnson:</strong> Well then, let’s go take a look.</p> <p>(The group moves closer to the structure. Upon closer inspection, it is clear it is built differently than the others.)</p> <p><strong>Lt. Johnson:</strong> Private Miller, can you go knock on the door?**</p> <p><strong>Pvt. Miller:</strong> Yes Lieutenant.</p> <p>(Miller walks up and knocks on the front door.)</p> <p><strong>Unknown:</strong> Hello?</p> <p>(A human male opens the front door. The physical appearance of the individual does not appear to have been painted.)</p> <p><strong>Unknown:</strong> Who are you? It’s not often that I get visitors.**</p> <p><strong>Pvt. Miller:</strong> How did you get in this place?</p> <p><strong>Unknown:</strong> What do you mean?</p> <p><strong>Pvt. Miller:</strong> Are there any others like you?</p> <p><strong>Unknown:</strong> You sure are asking a lot of questions. Do you want to come inside?</p> <p><strong>Pvt. Miller:</strong> Why not?</p> <p>(Pvt. Miller enters the structure. Inside is a sitting area.)</p> <p><strong>Unknown:</strong> Coffee?</p> <p><strong>Pvt. Miller:</strong> No thanks.</p> <p><strong>Unknown:</strong> Shame. I make it myself. Alright. Now that I’m comfortable, I get it you have some questions for me?</p> <p><strong>Pvt. Miller:</strong> That is correct.</p> <p><strong>Unknown:</strong> Spit it out then.</p> <p><strong>Pvt. Miller:</strong> Are there other people here?</p> <p><strong>Unknown:</strong> You would be the first in a few years. But yes, there are other people in this ‘realm’.</p> <p><strong>Pvt. Miller.</strong> And how did you get here?**</p> <p><strong>Unknown:</strong> I don’t know.</p> <p><strong>Pvt. Miller:</strong> Do you have a name?</p> <p><strong>Unknown:</strong> Jack.</p> <p><strong>Pvt. Miller:</strong> So, Jack, where were you before you got here?</p> <p><strong>Unknown:</strong> Chicago.</p> <p><strong>Pvt. Miller:</strong> Do you know where the other people here came from?</p> <p><strong>Unknown:</strong> I never asked them, that seemed a bit personal.</p> <p><strong>Pvt. Miller:</strong> Do you know where they are now?</p> <p><strong>Unknown:</strong> Most likely ok this realm, I don’t know where they are exactly though.</p> <p><strong>Pvt. Miller:</strong> I see. Well, I think I have to get going. We will meet again, Jack.</p> <p><strong>&lt;End Log&gt;</strong></p> <p><strong>End Note:</strong> Following this, the subject was designated as SCP-5487-2. See Addendum-XXXX-A</p> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class="collapsible-block"> <div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Exploration&nbsp;Log&nbsp;09</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none"> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Exploration&nbsp;Log&nbsp;09</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-content"> <div class="blockquote"> <p><strong>MTF Unit:</strong> Iota-27 (“Art Connoisseurs”)<br /> <strong>MTF Squad:</strong> Delta-2<br /> <strong>SCP-5487-1:</strong> Waterfall by M. C. Escher<br /> <strong>Task:</strong> Discover any deviations from baseline reality.</p> <p><strong>&lt;Begin Log&gt;</strong></p> <p>(Lt. Gibson Sgt. Grant Pvt. Jones and Pvt. Williams enter SCP-5487-1 on the pathway at the bottom center of the painting. Pvt. Jones attempts to step to the left, but instead walks backwards. A 90 degree turn changes the direction of movement the equivalent of 180 degrees.)</p> <p><strong>Pvt. Jones:</strong> What the [Data Explunged]</p> <p><strong>Lt. Gibson:</strong> Let’s orient ourselves before we begin the investigation.</p> <p>(The team moves around until they begin to comprehend how to love within SCP-5487-1.)</p> <p><strong>Lt. Gibson:</strong> Ok. I think that’s enough. Sgt. Grant, why don’t you look for a way up there.</p> <p>(Gibson points to the balcony above the archway to the left of where they are standing. Grant walks into the archway to the left of where they stand.)</p> <p><strong>Lt. Gibson:</strong> Pvt. Jones and Pvt. Williams, why don’t you go down those stairs to our right. Report back in 10 minutes.</p> <p>(Both privates walk away towards the staircase. As they do, Sgt. Grant exits the archway under the aquaduct.)</p> <p><strong>Sgt. Grant:</strong> Sir, there seems to be no way up from within the tunnel. I’ll have to look elsewhere.</p> <p>(Sgt. Grant looks over the railing along the staircase. The bottom is not visible.)</p> <p><strong>Lt. Gibson:</strong> Understood, thank you, Sarge.</p> <p>(Lt. Gibson enters the overgrown area at the bottom left of the painting. Nothing seems out of the ordinary except the size of the plants. 5 minutes later, Private Jones and Private Williams was back up the staircase.)</p> <p><strong>Pvt. Jones:</strong> The staircase is a deadend, sir. It ends at a sheer cliff off the side of the building.</p> <p><strong>Lt. Gibson:</strong> Thank you, Private.</p> <p>(Sgt. Grant appears on the balcony above the archway.)</p> <p><strong>Sgt. Grant:</strong> Letting down the rope, sir.</p> <p>(Sgt. Grant ties off a rope and lowers it off the balcony. The rest of the squad scales the wall using the rope. The aqueduct appears to zig-zag, but each corner is directly above another. It appears to be using the principle that turning 90 degrees moves it backwards, although the way it rises is unknown.)</p> <p><strong>Lt. Gibson:</strong> Alright, let’s take the measurements and get out of here.</p> <p>(The team gets to work doing preassigned expirements with the aqueduct.)</p> <p><strong>&lt;End Log&gt;</strong></p> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class="collapsible-block"> <div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Exploration&nbsp;Log&nbsp;13</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none"> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Exploration&nbsp;Log&nbsp;13</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-content"> <div class="blockquote"> <p><strong>MTF Unit:</strong> Iota-27 (“Art Connoisseurs”)<br /> <strong>MTF Squad:</strong> Delta-2<br /> <strong>SCP-5487-1:</strong> Melancholy Tunes on a Flemish Winter’s Day by Jos de Mey<br /> <strong>Task:</strong> Discover any deviations from baseline reality.<br /> <strong>Foreword:</strong> Due to a malfunction in the recording equipment, audio was not properly stored, and could not be recovered.</p> <p><strong>&lt;Begin Log&gt;</strong></p> <p>0:00: Lt. Gibson, Sgt. Grant, Pvt. Jones and Pvt. Williams exit the door in front of the middle pillar in the painting. The man sitting on the sidewalk playing the bagpipes looks questioningly at them, but continues playing.</p> <p>0:01: The group moves into the foreground of the painting, which appears to be a city square. No abnormalities other than what is present in the original painting are immediately noticeable.</p> <p>0:08: Lt. Gibson instructs Sgt. Grant and Pvt. Jones to investigate the street layout. When the group splits, Lt. Gibson and Pvt. Williams begin attempting to question the locals. However, everyone they attempt to speak to glances around and then briskly walks away.</p> <p>0:19: Sgt. Grant takes his 9th right turn, and has yet to cross back across his path. Pvt. Jones, however, took 8 left turns and, without crossing his own path, saw Sgt. Grant down the same street.</p> <p>0:22: Sgt. Grant and Pvt. Jones meet up and begin heading back.</p> <p>0:25: Pvt. Williams has found a resident that appears to be willing to speak, although lip reading software is unable to determine what it is saying.</p> <p>0:37: The group meets up again and heads back into the door, ending the exploration.</p> <p><strong>&lt;End Log&gt;</strong></p> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class="collapsible-block"> <div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Addendum-XXXX-A</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none"> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Addendum-XXXX-A</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-content"> <p>SCP-5487-2 appears to be a human male of European descent. It is estimated to be 5’ 7” tall, and weigh between 200-250 pounds. It is located within <span style="text-decoration: line-through;">Starry Night</span> every tested SCP-5487-1. SCP-5487 is unable to leave SCP-5487-1.</p> </div> </div> </div> <div class="colmod-block"> <ul> <li class="folded"> <ul> <li style="list-style: none">_</li> </ul> <div class="colmod-link-top"> <div class="foldable-list-container"><a href="javascript:;">Level 4 Access Required</a><a href="javascript:;">Access Granted</a></div> </div> <div class="colmod-content"> <div class="collapsible-block"> <div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Exploration&nbsp;Log&nbsp;14</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none"> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Exploration&nbsp;Log&nbsp;14</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-content"> <div class="blockquote"> <p><strong>MTF Unit:</strong> Iota-27 (“Art Connoisseurs”)<br /> <strong>MTF Squad:</strong> Delta-2<br /> <strong>SCP-5487-1:</strong> Ascending and Descending by MC Escher<br /> <strong>Task:</strong> Locate and interview SCP-5487-2<br /> <strong>Foreword:</strong> This log was recovered from the person of Lt. Johnson. The log had been damaged by a bullet.</p> <p><strong>&lt;Begin Log&gt;</strong></p> <p>(Lt. Johnson, Sgt. Anderson, Pvt. Miller, and Pvt. Carter are standing on the lower staircase at the bottom right corner of the painting.)</p> <p><strong>Lt. Johnson:</strong> Miller, you're with me. Us two will take this side, you two take that side. Check back here every 10 minutes.</p> <p>(Lt. Johnson and Pvt. Miller begin clearing rooms on the right side. Sgt.Anderson and Pvt. Carter take the left side rooms.)</p> <p><strong>[Data Lost]</strong></p> <p><strong>Pvt. Miller:</strong> minutes sir, I think we should head back.</p> <p><strong>Lt. Johnson:</strong> Alright, let’s go see if Sgt. Anderson has found anything.</p> <p>(Miller and Johnson go back to the starting point. Anderson is nowhere to be found.)</p> <p><strong>Lt. Johnson:</strong> They aren't here yet, let’s wait 5 minutes and go look for them if they</p> <p><strong>[Data Lost]</strong></p> <p>(Johnson and Miller are standing outside of one of the rooms. Inside voices can be heard, but no words can be made out.)</p> <p><strong>Lt. Johnson:</strong> 3. 2. 1. Breach!</p> <p>(Lt. Johnson kicks open e door and inside Anderson and Carter are tied to wooden chairs. 5 armed men bearing no insignias are present. Johnson and Miller are able to fire 7shots before ducking back behind the wall. 2 men get injured and one is killed.)</p> <p><strong>Unknown:</strong> You, go find Captain. Tell him we are under attack.</p> <p>(Johnson looks back through the door and kills another combatant before being shot in the abdomen.)</p> <p><strong>[Data Lost]</strong></p> <p>(Johnson’s body was dragged from the building and left on the ground outside. While still recording, the camera does not reveal anything else.)</p> <p><strong>&lt;End Log&gt;</strong></p> </div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div> <div class="foldable-list-container"></div> </div> </li> </ul> </div> <div style="text-align: right;"></div> <p>by <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/gunpowder77" ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=5218923&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606185837" alt="Gunpowder77" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=5218923)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/gunpowder77" >Gunpowder77</a></span></p> 
